# No comments in source code

Do **not** add comments, JSDoc, or commented-out code in application source
(`backend/`, `frontend/` — `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`).

Intent lives in names, types, and tests — not in `//`, `/* */`, or `{/* */}`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
/** Returns the user by id. */
function getUser(id: string) {
  // fetch from the API
  return api.get(`/users/${id}`);
}

// ✅ GOOD
function getUserById(id: string) {
  return api.get(`/users/${id}`);
}
```

## Do not

- Narrate what the next line does
- Leave commented-out code
- Add JSDoc for public APIs, components, or DTOs
- Add JSX comments

## Exceptions (only these)

- Third-party or generated files — do not rewrite them to strip comments
- Markdown, Cursor rules, skills, and `docs/` — not source code
- Dockerfiles, Compose, and `.env.*.example` — comments allowed; English only
  (`language.mdc`)
- An `eslint-disable` / `ts-expect-error` directive **only** when config cannot
  express it; no extra explanation around it

When editing a file that already has comments, remove comments in the code you
touch. Do not run a repo-wide comment strip unless asked.
